windows: Han layout follows a Han language, the app's first

DirectWrite chose Han glyphs and fallback fonts by the user's locale
alone, so a Han user on an English-locale Windows got Japanese glyphs
for Chinese text. The user's first Han language now leads the layout,
and an app may name its own with set_text_language (upstream
zed@1663af41 unfixed; cf. ElyOffice gpui patch 0010, Ely R4.13).

Note: the DirectWrite faces behavioral test from the Ely patch needs a
real DirectWrite stack and is left to on-machine acceptance; the pure
han() classifier is unit-tested here.

